WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.133
Enjoy yourself. Welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.300
You're here. Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.200
Well, everyone loves good news.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.434
Guys, you want to hear some good news?

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:12.601
-Yeah! -This morning, President Biden

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:14.534
announced that after days of negotiations,

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:17.234
railroad companies and unions reached a deal

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:20.067
to avoid a national rail strike. Yeah.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.534
Thank goodness.

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.133
Yeah, the President helped broker a deal

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.400
that went down to the wire. All night long, Biden was like,

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.300
"I think I can, I think I can, I think I can."

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.033
There's no way that there could have been

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.534
a rail strike under Biden.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:36.534
I mean, he rode a train to work every day for 40 years.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.868
That'd be like a tanning-bed shortage under Trump.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.601
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.267
Yeah, a strike would have meant

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.133
lots of Amtrak delays and cancellations.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.133
And now that the strike has been avoided...

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.934
there will still be delays and cancellations.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.133
I mean, it's just...

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.567
I saw that Mike Pence was in the news.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.000
I guess he stopped at a college

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.601
and went to a basketball court and took a video.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.234
Look at the video he posted.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.868
Hey! Yeah.

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:08.100
He drained the shot. Yeah.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.534
In fact, Pence was so impressive,

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.467
he actually is starring in a new basketball movie...

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.200
It's unbelievable.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.234
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.133
[ Applause ]

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:22.367
Some business news. Walmart has a new online feature

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.200
where you upload a seminude photo of yourself,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.167
and then you can virtually try on the clothing

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:31.634
to see what it would look like on your body.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.300
Kind of weird when a company is like,

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.300
"Go ahead. Just send us your nudes."

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.667
You go -- Well, this is fun.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.968
The finalists for the National Toy Hall of Fame

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.300
have been announced.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.434
And some of the toys include Lite-Brite.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:46.133
Love Lite-bright.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.467
Pound Puppies. -Oh.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.434
-And Nerf. Of course, Nerf.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.601
[ Applause ]

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.367
Of course, there were a lot of toys

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.901
that failed to make the cut this year.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:59.634
Of course, first, there's Square Ball.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.567
Next up is 10-Volt Slinky. That's a tough one.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.067
And finally, of course, Mr. Mashed Potato Head.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.334
It's just -- They didn't make it this year.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.567
[ Applause ]

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.834
They didn't make it.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.300
You guys, before we go any further,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.767
I have to issue a quick apology.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.400
On Tuesday, we here at "The Tonight Show"

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.067
forgot to acknowledge a very important holiday.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.334
That's right.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.167
I'm talking about National Bald is Beautiful Day.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.033
It happened, and we didn't say anything,

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.200
so to anyone out there who celebrates,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.834
I just want to say that I'm sorry.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.667
I know it's a special day for you,

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:36.100
and you deserve to feel special.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.968
So, whoever you are,

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:42.234
I hope you had the best, shiniest, smoothest day,

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:44.868
even if you're hiding under an obvious toupée.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.367
Uh, moving on. Here we go.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.601
Some -- Some sports news.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.834
Tonight was the debut of "Thursday Night Football"

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.501
on Amazon Prime Video.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.434
It's a pairing -- It's a pairing

00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:00.133
that actually makes more sense than you think. Watch this.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:03.601
-This fall, Amazon is the home of "Thursday Night Football."

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:07.968
Because only Amazon can bring you the best throws...

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.634
...the best tackles...

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.300
...and, of course, Daaa Bears.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.534
-Unh!

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.701
-Amazon. We deliver the action straight to you.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.801
-Yeah. Isn't that -- That's perfect. I think it's perfect.

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:28.000
[ Applause ]

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.100
Oh, and finally, you guys, did you hear about the new --

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.901
this new smoked-sausage recall?

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.534
It's not good. Check this out.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:38.133
-And we have a recall alert for you tonight

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.300
on a product you may have in your freezer.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.434
Sunset Farm Foods is recalling

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:46.000
their Georgia Special chicken and pork smoked sausage.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.067
-What?! Aw, man!

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.767
I just bought a pack of that for my barbecue this weekend.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:53.067
-I'm sorry about that, Tariq. -It's okay.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.067
I've still got some other meats at home.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.033
I'm talking fresh ground beef,

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.801
ground chuck, and ground sirloins.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.467
-That sounds pretty good. -Yeah, yeah.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:04.434
-I got them today at Schnucks on Mid Rivers Mall Drive.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:05.901
I forget when I picked them up.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.634
I think it was sometime after 10:15 in the morning,

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.868
but it was definitely before 2:30 in the afternoon.

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.901
-Oh.

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:16.300
-Oh, what? -Roll the clip.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.934
-Schnucks is recalling ground beef sold in its store

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.367
on Mid Rivers Mall Drive.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:23.067
This recall is for fresh ground beef, ground chuck,

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.000
and ground sirloin sold today

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.267
between 10:15 in the morning and 2:30 in the afternoon.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.667
-What?! You've got to be kidding me!

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:32.234
-I'm sorry about that, Tariq.

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:34.467
-Man, I was gonna make surf and turf!

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.334
I guess I'll just have surf.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:39.334
-That still sounds pretty good. -Yeah. You know me.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:42.334
Always got Bumble Bee smoked clams in my kitchen.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.300
I'm a certified seafood fan.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.567
-Seafood fans may want to take a close look inside the kitchen.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.634
Bumble Bee is voluntarily recalling

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.901
some of its smoked clams for safety concerns.

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.167
-Come on! -I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.667
I'm sure you'll figure something out for your barbecue.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:01.467
-Whatever. No surf, no turf. I don't need to cook anything.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.667
I'll just chill in my backyard.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:07.200
Maybe kick back in one of my new outdoor metal hanging chairs.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.000
I got them at TJX.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.601
-Now to a recall alert for TJX customers.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.367
The department-store chain is recalling

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:17.934
roughly 5,200 outdoor metal hanging chairs.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.200
-Fine, but if I can't cook or sit,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.067
I'm still going to get the yard looking fresh

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.701
with my new Sun Joe cordless lawn mower.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.901
-That's cool. -Yeah, I usually try to get

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.367
the whole family out on the lawn

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.133
and then line the kids up around me.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.901
They like to lay down in the grass and watch Daddy mow.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:36.567
-We have a recall alert for Sun Joe cordless lawn mowers.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:40.033
The company says the mower blade can detach unexpectedly.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:41.601
-I'm over it, man!

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:44.567
I'm just gonna listen to some music on my new headphones.

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:45.734
-Oh, cool.

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.300
What brand are those? -HearMuffs.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.868
-The FDA is recalling tens of thousands of HearMuffs

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.868
over exploding batteries.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:56.734
They can rupture, burst, and then cause burn injuries.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:59.000
-[Bleep] Damn it! That's it! I'm out of here!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.267
-Come on, now. Hey.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:01.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.534
-Alright. Tariq's gonna cool down a little bit.

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:07.300
A lot of stuff. A rough weekend. We have a great show tonight.

